#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:4
msgid "WebXR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:6
msgid "WebXR is a web standard for delivering XR experiences right from a web browser, without the user needing to install anything. Godot has built-in support for WebXR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:11
msgid "As this uses the HTML export WebXR requires the use of the compatibility renderer. Godot currently requires multiview support for stereo rendering which is not available on all WebXR capable devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:15
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:17
msgid "Setting up WebXR is a little different because your application always starts as a normal non-XR webpage. We thus define a 2D UI on our main page that includes a button that will switch to XR."
msgstr ""

