msgid "Make sure the \"Enable WebXR\" button's ``button_pressed`` signal calls the ``_on_enter_webxr_button_pressed`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:121
msgid "In the code above we attempt to use the ``local-floor`` reference spaces. This reference spaces assumes gameplay where we need to know the player's height from the floor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:124
msgid "For games where the player is seated inside of a vehicle, such as flight sims or racing games, the reference space ``local`` may be more appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:128
msgid "Controller input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:130
msgid "The input system in WebXR works against a fixed set of inputs that obfuscate the actual hardware being used. In order to allow for code to be portable between a WebXR and OpenXR application these inputs are mapped to actions that overlap with the default action map used by our OpenXR interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/webxr_intro.rst:132
msgid "There are small differences such as WebXR separating touchpad and thumbsticks as separate inputs, instead of the primary and secondary input setup found in our default OpenXR action map."
msgstr ""

